1
00:06:10,588 --> 00:06:16,588
A passion. An obsession. A love that destroyed everyone it touched.

2
00:12:21,176 --> 00:12:27,176
Wuthering Heights is a drama, romance film directed by Peter Kosminsky.

3
00:18:31,764 --> 00:18:37,764
Young orphan Heathcliff is adopted by the wealthy Earnshaw family
and moves into their estate, Wuthering Heights.

4
00:24:42,352 --> 00:24:48,352
Soon, the new resident falls for his compassionate foster sister, Cathy.

5
00:30:52,941 --> 00:30:58,941
The two share a remarkable bond that seems unbreakable until Cathy, feeling the pressure of social
convention, suppresses her feelings and marries Edgar Linton, a man of means who befits her stature.

6
00:37:03,529 --> 00:37:09,529
Heathcliff vows to win her back.

7
00:43:14,117 --> 00:43:20,117
Cathy / Catherine Linton, played by Juliette Binoche.

8
00:49:24,705 --> 00:49:30,705
Heathcliff, played by Ralph Fiennes.

9
00:55:35,294 --> 00:55:41,294
Ellen Dean, played by Janet McTeer.

10
01:01:45,882 --> 01:01:51,882
Isabella Linton, played by Sophie Ward.

11
01:07:56,470 --> 01:08:02,470
Edgar Linton, played by Simon Shepherd.

12
01:14:07,058 --> 01:14:13,058
Hindley Earnshaw, played by Jeremy Northam.

13
01:20:17,647 --> 01:20:23,647
Emily Brontë's Wuthering Heights is a 1992 historical film adaptation of Emily
Brontë's 1847 novel Wuthering Heights directed by Peter Kosminsky.

14
01:26:28,235 --> 01:26:34,235
It marked Ralph Fiennes's film debut.

15
01:32:38,823 --> 01:32:44,823
This particular film is notable for including the oft-omitted second
generation story of the children of Cathy, Hindley and Heathcliff.

16
01:38:49,411 --> 01:38:55,411
The tone is emotional.
